posture coverage, without naming a specific upstream directory. The other
service guides name AWS best-practice references rather than an upstream
directory; this is not a determination that they are independent works.

For this preliminary review, the upstream repository was inspected at commit
`4ba3146a7593b72ce740dadccb1e05ae599e43e7` on 2026-11-23. The owner has not
identified the upstream revision actually used during development, so this
snapshot is a comparison reference, not a claimed original source revision.
The review inventoried guide references and spot-checked Lambda and EFS
against upstream service material; it did not establish line-by-line
provenance for all check text or all other documentation.

The owner estimates development began in early July 2026. Upstream commit
`87cf4561cb196c33dec30ce42314f0467a3c9ad0`, dated 2026-07-08, was also
checked as a possible period reference. The referenced service directories
were present at that commit, and its LICENSE and NOTICE match the later
snapshot. This does not establish which upstream revision was actually used.

For example, the Lambda guide's dead-letter-queue and code-signing topics
also occur in upstream `services/lambda_/lambda.reporter.json`. The EFS
guide's encryption, backup and lifecycle topics also occur in upstream
`services/efs/efs.reporter.json`. Topic overlap alone does not establish
copying or the origin of individual wording.

The upstream notice mentions AdminLTE. Its notice is retained as part of the
